1 DISMOUNT

   Dismounts the volume mounted on a device, writing what is pending and
   closing the container file.  The device stays, and another volume can
   be mounted on it.

   Format

     DISMOUNT device-name

2 Parameter

 device-name

   The device, such as DUA1; a colon after it is optional.  A logical
   name, such as the DISK$label name MOUNT defined, is translated first.

2 Description

   Dismounting a device with nothing mounted on it is an error, and so
   is dismounting a volume with files open (a process the console
   stopped may still have some): close them, or STOP the process, first.
   The system volume can't be dismounted, nor the page file's volume.
   When govax exits, every volume is dismounted.

2 Examples

   1.$ DISMOUNT DUA1

     Dismounts the volume on DUA1.
